				Import the JUnit BOM so every junit-jupiter-* and junit-platform-*
				artifact (api, params, engine, commons, launcher, ...) is locked to
				a single version. Without this, transitive deps such as
				mockito-junit-jupiter drag in an older junit-jupiter-api (e.g.
				5.13.4) and Surefire's JUnit Platform alignment check then refuses
				to fork the test JVM (wrapped NoClassDefFoundError).
			-->
			<dependency>
				<groupId>org.junit</groupId>
				<artifactId>junit-bom</artifactId>
				<version>${junit.jupiter.version}</version>
				<type>pom</type>
				<scope>import</scope>
			</dependency>
			<!--
				Force Bouncy Castle to ${bouncyCastle.version} across all modules.
				Without this, io.minio:minio drags in a vulnerable bcprov-jdk18on
